  triage:description "Prior-sprint triage records RBP-F001 and RBQA-F001 (AO.1-era) appear resolved in the current code but remain marked open in the triage store (.triage/phase-ao2/findings/). Evidence: RBP-F001 (PeerWireMode.security field access control) is fixed — the field is now private on crates/atm-core/src/peer_wire.rs:39, accessible only via a const method. RBQA-F001 (PeerWireSecurity substring collision) is fixed — the AK.2 retirement guard now matches exact symbols, not substrings, verified by test ak2_retirement_guard_matches_symbols_not_substrings() passing on PeerWireSecurity. Remediation: formally close them (via Resolution event, team-lead action) with reference to current-commit evidence in feature/pao-s3-runtime-peer-wire-mode branch (head_sha e6a428355253de23a428bac2f047180ec95dfc7c). This is a team-lead closure action, not a code-fix task for arch-ctm." ;
